# Every vendored file, once. tools/xemu-vendor.py sync copies exactly these from each source at its pin into
# external/<source>/<path>, then applies external/xemu-vendor/patches/*.patch in order; xemu-vendor.py check (CI, every
# push) proves external/ == pinned upstream + patches and caps the patches; build.ps1 compiles the .c files listed here
# and only those. A path appears once per section. "@<source> <url> <commit>" opens a section; paths follow.
# The cap is on the patches: changed lines and distinct patched files. Expected use is zero; raising it is a reviewed
# edit of this line, and each patch says in its header why the shim cannot absorb it instead.
